ander">Lysander</a> defeats the Athenian fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-notium">Notium</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">356 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herostratus">Herostratus</a> burns the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-artemis">Temple of Artemis</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">334 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> restores democracy and gives the Persian tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 290 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachus">Lysimachus</a> moves the city to a new site and renames it Arsinoeia</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">133 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attalus-iii">Attalus III</a> bequeaths <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pergamon">Pergamon</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a></span></li></ol>
